### **Goal Model Decomposition**  
---

#### **Goals Table**  

| Name       | Text                                                                 | Runtime                          | Goal Type  | Relation     |
|------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------|------------|--------------|
| G1         | Deliver food from kitchen to inpatient room on order-by-order basis | -                                | Perform    | -            |
| G2         | Handle food delivery method (direct placement or tray fetching)     | FALLBACK(G2.1, G2.2)             | Perform    | AND          |
| G2.1       | Deliver food directly to inpatient room table                       | -                                | Perform    | -            |
| G2.2       | Allow inpatient to fetch food from robot tray                       | FALLBACK(AT1, AT2, AT3)          | Perform    | -            |
| G3         | Check if inpatient can fetch food from tray                         | (Query on patient record)        | Query      | AND          |
| G4         | Track meal retrieval by inpatient                                   | -                                | Achieve    | AND          |
| G5         | Retrieve dirty dishes from inpatient room                           | FALLBACK(G5.1, G5.2)             | Perform    | AND          |
| G5.1       | Retrieve dishes unassisted by robot                                 | -                                | Perform    | -            |
| G5.2       | Retrieve dishes with cooperation (robot/robot + human)              | #                                  | Perform    | -            |

---

#### **Tasks Table**  

| Name      | Text                                                                 | Relation     | Location         | Number of Robots |
|-----------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------|------------------|------------------|
| AT1       | Place food on inpatient room table using manipulation skill          | AND          | Inpatient Room   | [1]              |
| AT2       | Alert if wrong meal is retrieved by inpatient                        | AND          | Inpatient Room   | [1]              |
| AT3       | Indicate which meal corresponds to the inpatient                     | AND          | Inpatient Room   | [1]              |
| AT4       | Open room door with cooperation (robot/human)                        | AND          | Inpatient Room   | [1,2]            |
| AT5       | Retrieve dirty dishes from inpatient room                            | AND          | Inpatient Room   | [1]              |
| AT6       | Signal to robot if person can open the door                          | AND          | Inpatient Room   | [1]              |

---

### **Logical Relationships**  
- **G1 -> G2, G5 [AND]**  
- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [FALLBACK]**  
- **G2.2 -> AT1, AT2, AT3 [OR]**  
- **G3 -> Query on patient record [AND]**  
- **G4 -> AT2, AT3 [AND]**  
- **G5 -> G5.1, G5.2 [FALLBACK]**  
- **G5.2 -> AT4, AT6 [OR]**  

---

### **Summary**  
The system decomposes into two main goals: **food delivery** (G1) and **dirty dish retrieval** (G5). Food delivery uses a fallback between direct placement (G2.1) and tray fetching (G2.2), which itself depends on cooperation tasks (AT1–AT3). Dish retrieval (G5) uses a fallback between unassisted (G5.1) and cooperative (G5.2) methods, with AT4/AT6 handling door access. All goals are linked via AND/OR relationships to ensure robustness against uncertainty (e.g., patient capability, human availability).
